# Backend Server Configuration
PORT=8000
HOST=127.0.0.1
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,http://127.0.0.1:5173,https://smart-document-generator-acm-svnit.vercel.app

# Security Secrets (generate separate random values; never use these examples)
JWT_SECRET_KEY=replace-with-a-long-random-secret
ADMIN_BOOTSTRAP_SECRET=replace-with-a-long-random-one-time-bootstrap-secret
ADMIN_BOOTSTRAP_EMAIL=your-account@dept.svnit.ac.in
# Supabase PostgreSQL connection string. Keep this backend-only and use the
# Supabase connection string suitable for your network (Render should use the
# direct or session-pooler URL with SSL enabled).
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:5432/postgres?sslmode=require
# Local tests/development only; set SMARTDOCS_DB_BACKEND=sqlite and a path.
SMARTDOCS_DB_BACKEND=postgres
SMARTDOCS_DATABASE_PATH=
# Render must use a private Supabase Storage bucket for durable generated files.
SMARTDOCS_STORAGE_BACKEND=supabase
SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=
SUPABASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=smartdocs-private

# Firebase Admin credentials are backend-only. Set the service-account JSON as a
# Render secret (single-line JSON), never in Vercel or a committed file.
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=smartdocs-svnit-6904c
FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON={}
ALLOWED_EMAIL_DOMAINS=svnit.ac.in,svnit.acm.org
PUBLIC_REGISTRATION_ROLES=author
PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://smart-document-generator-acm-svnit.vercel.app

# Optional: these are used only by the separate document distribution feature.
# Firebase Authentication handles all auth and verification emails.
RESEND_API_KEY=
EMAIL_FROM=

# Optional intelligent extraction fallback
GEMINI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
